# Available Tools in This Container

You are running in a Docker container with full sudo access.

## Languages & Runtimes
- Go 1.26 — /usr/local/go/bin/go
- Python 3.12 (system) + uv, pyenv-managed Python 3.12.11 also available
- Node.js 22 LTS with npm

## Go Tools
- golangci-lint, gopls, dlv, staticcheck, gomodifytags, impl, gotests, gofumpt

## Python Tools
- flake8, black, isort, autoflake, pyright, mypy, vulture, pytest, pytest-cov, pipenv, poetry

## Node.js Tools
- eslint, prettier, typescript, ts-node, yarn, pnpm, nodemon, pm2
- create-react-app, @vue/cli, @angular/cli, express-generator, newman, http-server, serve, lighthouse, @storybook/cli

## Infrastructure & DevOps
- terraform, kubectl, helm, docker + compose + buildx, gh

## Databases & Data
- sqlite3, postgresql-client (psql), mysql-client, redis-tools (redis-cli)

## Shell & System Tools
- git, curl, wget, httpie, jq
- tree, fd-find (fdfind), ripgrep (rg), bat, eza, silversearcher-ag (ag)
- shellcheck, shfmt, tmux, htop

## C/C++ Tools
- gcc, g++, make, cmake, clang-format, valgrind, gdb, strace, ltrace

## Notes
- Passwordless sudo access
- Docker socket may be mounted for docker-in-docker. The workspace path inside
  the container matches the host path, so `docker run -v "$PWD/data:/data"` from
  within resolves correctly on the host.
- pyenv at /usr/local/pyenv, Go tools at /usr/local/bin
- `~/.claude/bin` is in PATH — drop custom scripts there.
- `/aicodebox-init.d/*.sh` scripts fire once on first container create.

## IMPORTANT
If you need to overwrite this CLAUDE.md, first save the container environment
notes above to `~/.claude/CONTAINER.md` so you don't lose the container-specific
context. This file is regenerated on first container create only.
